diff --git a/INSTALL_EN.md b/INSTALL_EN.md
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+# Triton-Ascend Installation Guide
+
+This guide provides step-by-step instructions for installing Triton-Ascend on Ascend NPU platforms.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)
+- [Quick Install (via pip)](#quick-install-via-pip)
+- [Build from Source](#build-from-source)
+- [Verify Installation](#verify-installation)
+- [Troubleshooting](#troubleshooting)
+
+---
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+###System Requirements
+- **Operating System**: Linux based OS (x86_64 or ARM64)
+- **Python**: 3.9 - 3.11
+- **GCC**: >= 9.4.0
+- **GLIBC**: >= 2.27
+
+### Install System Dependencies
+
+```bash
+# Update package list
+sudo apt update
+
+# Install required packages
+sudo apt install -y zlib1g-dev clang-15 lld-15 ccache
+
+# Optional: Configure clang-15 as default (if you have multiple clang versions)
+sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/clang clang /usr/bin/clang-15 20
+sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/clang++ clang++ /usr/bin/clang++-15 20
+sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/lld lld /usr/bin/lld-15 20
+```
+
+### Install Python Dependencies
+
+```bash
+# Install build dependencies
+pip install ninja cmake wheel pybind11
+
+# Install runtime dependencies
+pip install attrs==24.2.0 numpy==1.26.4 scipy==1.13.1 \
+            decorator==5.1.1 psutil==6.0.0 pytest==8.3.2 \
+            pytest-xdist==3.6.1 pyyaml
+
+# Install PyTorch for Ascend NPU
+pip install torch==2.6.0 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
+pip install torch_npu==2.6.0
+```
+
+---
+
+## Build from Source
+
+Follow these steps if you need to modify Triton-Ascend or want the latest development version.
+
+### Step 1: Clone the Repository
+
+```bash
+git clone https://gitcode.com/Ascend/triton-ascend.git
+cd triton-ascend
+git submodule update --init --depth 1
+# this will initialize both the `ascendnpu-ir` and `triton` third party
+```
+
+### Step 2: Build LLVM
+
+Triton-Ascend requires a specific version of LLVM with MLIR support.
+
+```bash
+# Clone LLVM repository
+cd ~
+git clone --no-checkout https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project.git
+cd llvm-project
+
+# Checkout the specific commit required by Triton-Ascend
+git checkout b5cc222d7429fe6f18c787f633d5262fac2e676f
+
+# Set installation path
+export LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX=$HOME/llvm-install
+
+# Configure LLVM build
+mkdir build && cd build
+cmake ../llvm \
+  -G Ninja \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
+  -DLLVM_ENABLE_ASSERTIONS=ON \
+  -DLLVM_ENABLE_PROJECTS="mlir;llvm;lld" \
+  -DLLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD="host;NVPTX;AMDGPU" \
+  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=${LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX} \
+  -DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=clang \
+  -DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=clang++
+
+# Build and install
+ninja install -j$(nproc)
+```
+
+> **Note**: If using GCC instead of clang, you may need to add `-DLLVM_ENABLE_LLD=ON` if you encounter linker errors.
+
+### Step 3: Build Triton-Ascend
+
+```bash
+cd ~/triton-ascend
+
+# Set LLVM path
+export LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX=$HOME/llvm-install
+
+# Build and install
+LLVM_SYSPATH=${LLVM_INSTALL_PREFIX} \
+TRITON_PLUGIN_DIRS=./ascend \
+TRITON_BUILD_WITH_CCACHE=true \
+TRITON_BUILD_WITH_CLANG_LLD=true \
+TRITON_BUILD_PROTON=OFF \
+TRITON_WHEEL_NAME="triton_ascend" \
+TRITON_APPEND_CMAKE_ARGS="-DTRITON_BUILD_UT=OFF" \
+python3 setup.py install --user
+```
+
+#### Build Options
+
+- `LLVM_SYSPATH`: Path to LLVM installation
+- `TRITON_PLUGIN_DIRS`: Path to Ascend backend plugin
+- `TRITON_BUILD_WITH_CCACHE`: Use ccache to speed up rebuilds
+- `TRITON_BUILD_WITH_CLANG_LLD`: Use clang and lld for building
+- `TRITON_BUILD_PROTON`: Set to OFF to skip Proton profiler
+
+---
+
+## Verify Installation
+
+### Test 1: Check Module Import
+
+```bash
+python3 -c "import triton; print('Triton version:', triton.__version__)"
+python3 -c "import triton.language.extra.ascend as al; print('al.Scope available:', hasattr(al, 'Scope'))"
+```
+
+### Test 2: Test al.Scope Syntax (without NPU hardware)
+
+```bash
+# Set environment variable to skip NPU backend loading
+export TORCH_DEVICE_BACKEND_AUTOLOAD=0
+
+# Run the al.Scope test script
+python3 generate_mlir_frontend_only.py
+```

